(2) The membership composition of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) among others consists of:

a. elements of the Regional Government;
b. academics;
c. legal experts;
d. psychologists;
e. psychiatrists;
f. religious leaders; and
g. community elements.
(3) The principal duties of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) are: a. providing protection to women and children; and b. improving the quality of life of women and children.
(4) Further provisions regarding the establishment of P2TP2A shall be stipulated by Regent's Decree.

