Article 4

The objectives of the protection of women and children from violence are: a. to prevent violence against women and children;

b. to eliminate all forms of violence against women and children; c. to protect and provide a sense of security for women and children; d. to provide services to women and children who are victims of violence;

e. to carry out rehabilitation and reintegration of women and children who are victims of violence; and

f. to carry out empowerment of women and children who are victims of violence.

Article 16

(1) Prevention as referred to in Article 15 letter a, is implemented by way of:

a. forming a network in efforts to prevent violence;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
c. establishing a violence prevention system;
d. conducting socialization about laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence; and
e. providing knowledge about prevention and mechanisms for addressing violence against women and children.
(2) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented in an integrated manner by the Regency Regional Apparatus and related agencies that have main tasks and functions in the fields of:
a. women's empowerment and child protection;
b. education;
c. health;
d. social affairs;
e. labor;
f. youth and sports; and
g. mental and spiritual.
(3) In addition to being implemented by the Regency Regional Apparatus and related agencies as referred to in paragraph (2), prevention is also implemented by:
a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. the community, NGOs, community organizations, social organizations and religious organizations; and
c. the business community.

